From 367f854c120a791a181da26120f47c8439eea774 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Krueckel <hi@felkru.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:53:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 38/54] Run bash and fish over the remote PTY, and answer the
 shell's terminal queries

The host app names its shell in the session endpoint (`shell=bash`); remote_tty uses it for the
session's shell type and init line instead of always assuming zsh:
- bash gets the init script through `eval`; fish too, then reads Warp's bootstrap through
  `head -c N | source` instead of its line editor, which redraws the growing `begin ... end`
  block for every chunk typed (over 15 s).
- fish sets WARP_HONOR_PS1 with `set -gx`.
- The init line waits for the shell's first output and 100 ms of quiet (at most 2 s): until the
  line editor reads input, the terminal keeps only 1024 bytes of a typed line (MAX_CANON).

The parser's replies to terminal queries (device attributes, cursor position, colors) went to
io::sink(); they now go to the shell like on desktop. fish 4 waited 10 s at startup for one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
